# CHANGELOG

## 8.8.12

fix: [PAYMCLOUD-1384] Probe defaults and HAProxy backend annotations

- default `periodSeconds: 10` and `failureThreshold: 3` (the Kubernetes defaults) for `livenessProbe`,
  `readinessProbe` and `startupProbe`: with 1 and 1 a single slow response restarted the container.
  ⚠️ Releases that rely on the defaults now detect a failing container after ~30s instead of ~1s
- a single helper renders the HAProxy backend annotations of the main and canary Services
  (`ingress.haproxy.backendAnnotations`, otherwise the `rewriteTarget` path rewrite snippet): the canary Services
  no longer skip the rewrite when `ingress.haproxy.path` is empty

## 8.8.11

fix: [PAYMCLOUD-1383] Robustness

- every resource gets a namespace: `namespace`, falling back to the release namespace (it was rendered empty when
  `namespace` was not set)
- default `securityContext.capabilities.drop` is `ALL` (it was `all`, not recognized by Pod Security Admission `restricted`)
- `podDisruptionBudget`: exactly one of `minAvailable` and `maxUnavailable` is required, the chart fails otherwise
  (it rendered a PodDisruptionBudget without constraints); `minAvailable: 0` is now rendered; the PodDisruptionBudget
  gets the common labels.
  ⚠️ `podDisruptionBudget.create: true` without `minAvailable`/`maxUnavailable` now fails: the old default
  `minAvailable: 0` was ignored, set it explicitly
- the canary merges of `envConfig`/`envSecret` and the non critical `nodeSelector` no longer modify `.Values`
- legacy nginx canary: the merged `envConfig` values in the ConfigMap are quoted strings (numbers and booleans made the
  API server reject it) and the canary `envConfig` is used even when the stable `envConfig` is empty

## 8.8.10

fix: [PAYMCLOUD-1382] externalConfigMapValues and NOTES.txt

- `externalConfigMapValues`: default and documentation now describe the supported format
  `<configmap name>: {<ENV VAR NAME>: <key>}` (the old comment suggested a list that rendered invalid env vars);
  a non empty list now fails with an explicit error, the old empty default `configMaps: []` is ignored
- `NOTES.txt`: uses the first `service.ports` entry instead of the non existing `service.port`, and the chart
  `namespace` (falling back to the release namespace)

## 8.8.9

fix: [PAYMCLOUD-1381] SecretProviderClass

- the SecretProviderClass and the `secrets-store-inline` volume are created only when at least one secret is configured:
  with the defaults the chart rendered a SecretProviderClass with an empty Key Vault and the pod stayed in `ContainerCreating`
- a Key Vault secret referenced more than once (`envSecret`, `initContainerEnvSecret`, `providedVolumeMount.envSecret`) is loaded once:
  duplicated objects were rejected by the CSI driver
- empty `clientID`, `keyvaultName` and `tenantId` are rendered as empty strings instead of `null`

## 8.8.8

fix: [PAYMCLOUD-1380] HAProxy canary pod labels

- the pods of the HAProxy canary Deployment get the `azure.workload.identity/use` label (when `azure.workloadIdentityEnabled`)
  and the `critical` label, like the stable pods: without the first one the workload identity token was not injected
  and the canary application could not authenticate to Azure

## 8.8.7

fix: [PAYMCLOUD-1379] Init containers

- `tmpVolumeMount` is optional: an init container without it failed with a nil pointer error
- `image.pullPolicy` and `image.tag` are optional, `name` and `image.repository` are required with an explicit error
- `volumeMounts` is rendered only when there is something to mount
- new per init container fields: `env` (Kubernetes EnvVar list, added after `initContainerEnvConfig`/`initContainerEnvSecret`),
  `volumeMounts` (any pod volume: Key Vault secrets, PVCs, config maps, Azure File shares), `securityContext` and `resources`.
  securityContext and resources are not inherited from the main container

## 8.8.6

fix: [PAYMCLOUD-1378] azureFile

- new `azureFile.mounts[].mountPath`: when set, the share is also mounted in the main container (before the volume was
  created but never mounted); without it the volume can still be mounted by the init containers
- new `azureFile.secretName` to use an existing Secret with a custom name (default `<fullname>-azure-file`)
- `readOnly` defaults to `false`, `name` and `shareName` are required with an explicit error
- `azureFile` documented in `values.yaml` and README

## 8.8.5

fix: [PAYMCLOUD-1377] Deployment replicas

- with autoscaling disabled, `deployment.replicas` is always applied (on upgrade the current replicas of the
  Deployment were kept, so changing it had no effect); `deployment.replicas: 0` is allowed
- with autoscaling enabled, the replicas set by KEDA are kept on upgrade, including 0 (scale to zero was reset to 1),
  and the live Deployment is looked up in the chart `namespace`

## 8.8.4

fix: [PAYMCLOUD-1376] Environment variable values as strings

- `envConfig` and `initContainerEnvConfig` values are rendered as quoted strings in the ConfigMaps: numbers and
  booleans (e.g. `PORT: 8080`) made the API server reject the ConfigMap
- canary env values and `externalConfigMapValues` keys are rendered as strings too

## 8.8.3

fix: [PAYMCLOUD-1375] canaryDelivery values

- `canaryDelivery.image`, `canaryDelivery.envConfig` and `canaryDelivery.envSecret` are declared at `canaryDelivery`
  level in `values.yaml`, where the templates read them: they were nested under `canaryDelivery.ingress`, so enabling
  `canaryDelivery.create` with the defaults failed with a nil pointer error

chore: [PAYMCLOUD-1374] Chart tests in CI (no chart change)

- helm-unittest suites and kubeconform validation of the `ci/` scenarios on every pull request (`Chart Tests` workflow)
- chart `.helmignore` to keep the tests out of the packaged chart

